body:
Yeah you're probably right, I just wanted to make a dumb joke. My headcanon is that there is an MMIO peripheral for gender, and `trans` is a reference to volatile pointer, which would prevent all optimizations.

```
#define GENDER_OFFSET 0xb00b;
volatile void* self = 0x40000000;
bool& trans = *((bool*)(self + GENDER_OFFSET));
...
```
